you won't see the spots. OK?

253
00:10:53.652 --> 00:10:56.115
And maybe have some
and relax. OK?

254
00:10:56.215 --> 00:10:58.638
Tonight's gonna be great.
Everybody likes Breonna.

255
00:10:58.738 --> 00:11:00.116
Mm-hmm. even though
she doesn't laugh

256
00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:01.322
at any of my jokes.

257
00:11:01.422 --> 00:11:02.679
I mean. everybody loves Breonna.

258
00:11:02.703 --> 00:11:04.365
I'm not worried about that.

259
00:11:04.465 --> 00:11:07.089
Wait. Does Breonna
not like us?

260
00:11:07.189 --> 00:11:08.851
Are we not mature enough
for her?

261
00:11:08.951 --> 00:11:10.649
Jordan: So that's why she
doesn't think I'm funny.

262
00:11:10.673 --> 00:11:12.010
You know. those
elite types. they just...

263
00:11:12.034 --> 00:11:13.897
they never get
my simple folk humour.

264
00:11:13.997 --> 00:11:16.380
You know what. I don't like
either one of you right now.

265
00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:17.897
And for the record.
Breonna didn't grow up

266
00:11:17.921 --> 00:11:19.704
swimming in some pool
in Beverly Hills

267
00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:21.626
like some "simple folk" I know.

268
00:11:21.726 --> 00:11:23.406
She's not too different
from me. all right.

269
00:11:23.488 --> 00:11:26.392
so y'all can kill
all the fancy talk.

270
00:11:26.492 --> 00:11:28.394
[Doorbell rings]

271
00:11:28.494 --> 00:11:30.637
And now she's here.

272
00:11:30.737 --> 00:11:32.719
OK. OK. And what is this?

273
00:11:32.819 --> 00:11:35.402
A little smoked duck
with some cherry glaze.

274
00:11:35.502 --> 00:11:36.724
Sorry. girl.

275
00:11:36.824 --> 00:11:38.686
The only thing Coop told me
about this dinner

276
00:11:38.786 --> 00:11:40.725
was that it was tonight
and that we had to hurry up.

277
00:11:40.749 --> 00:11:42.771
So I hope this will do.

278
00:11:42.871 --> 00:11:44.413
I mean. Charcoal
& Ash? Nice!

279
00:11:44.513 --> 00:11:45.811
I did not know that
they did takeout.

280
00:11:45.835 --> 00:11:47.016
Breonna: You know. they do

281
00:11:47.116 --> 00:11:49.259
when your firm handled
their payroll case.

282
00:11:49.359 --> 00:11:50.701
Coop: All right. chill.

283
00:11:50.801 --> 00:11:52.258
You acting like you
never seen food before.

284
00:11:52.282 --> 00:11:53.962
Jordan: Hold on. now.
The boxes have vents.

285
00:11:54.004 --> 00:11:56.427
That is a clutch move.
Keeps the potatoes crispy.

286
00:11:56.527 --> 00:11:57.429
Ha!

287
00:11:57.529 --> 00:11:59.531
Very fancy.

288
00:12:05.538 --> 00:12:06.960
What's going on?

289
00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:10.084
Coop and Breonna are
treating us to dinner.

290
00:12:10.184 --> 00:12:14.409
Yeah. Preach and Amina
are on their way.

291
00:12:14.509 --> 00:12:17.132
Uh. you cool if I skip?
I'm not too hungry.

292
00:12:17.232 --> 00:12:19.050
I'm sorry. Do you smell
the truffle barbecue rub

293
00:12:19.074 --> 00:12:21.177
on those wings?

294
00:12:21.277 --> 00:12:23.340
Is everything OK?

295
00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.823
Yeah. I'm fine.
Uh. just a rough day.

296
00:12:25.923 --> 00:12:29.147
Ah. Well. you're about
to have a great weekend.

297
00:12:29.247 --> 00:12:30.628
I just got word that

298
00:12:30.728 --> 00:12:32.230
the assistant coach at Stanford

299
00:12:32.330 --> 00:12:33.512
will be at the showcase.

300
00:12:33.612 --> 00:12:35.114
-For real?
-Mm-hmm.

301
00:12:35.214 --> 00:12:37.072
That's great. but. Coach.
you know my test scores...

302
00:12:37.096 --> 00:12:38.398
I know. I know.

303
00:12:38.498 --> 00:12:40.080
And I can't promise
you anything.

304
00:12:40.180 --> 00:12:42.322
But when you impress
the hell out of him.

305
00:12:42.422 --> 00:12:43.804
like I know you will.

306
00:12:43.904 --> 00:12:45.887
maybe he'll tell the coach
you're someone

307
00:12:45.987 --> 00:12:48.129
worth reevaluating with
the admissions office.

308
00:12:48.229 --> 00:12:50.492
Thanks. Coach.

309
00:12:50.592 --> 00:12:52.374
I needed some good news today.

310
00:12:52.474 --> 00:12:53.474
[Sniffs]

311
00:12:53.516 --> 00:12:54.697
Just keep up the good work

312
00:12:54.797 --> 00:12:56.255
and there'll be more
to come. all right?

313
00:12:56.279 --> 00:12:59.423
Just like these wings.
Check that out.

314
00:12:59.523 --> 00:13:02.987
Bet you're hungry now.
We got wings!

315
00:13:03.087 --> 00:13:04.309
Coming in hot.

316
00:13:04.409 --> 00:13:05.626
Coop: Oh. wow.
Layla: Oh. great.

317
00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.652
[Indistinct chatter]

318
00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:16.203
KJ: Careful Jordan doesn't
try to steal those. too.

319
00:13:16.303 --> 00:13:18.205
We've been over this.

320
00:13:18.305 --> 00:13:19.767
Jordan did not steal my job.

321
00:13:19.867 --> 00:13:21.529
It was offered to him.

322
00:13:21.629 --> 00:13:23.632
Well. he could've said no.

323
00:13:24.793 --> 00:13:28.698
Anyway. how'd the meeting
go with that booster?

324
00:13:28.798 --> 00:13:30.059
[Chuckles softly]

325
00:13:30.159 --> 00:13:31.919
I think the only person
that hates the Bakers

326
00:13:32.002 --> 00:13:34.745
more than Cliff Mosely
is my dad.

327
00:13:34.845 --> 00:13:36.187
Why? What did he say?

328
00:13:36.287 --> 00:13:39.070
It was more of a gut feeling.

329
00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.954
Well. well. did he say
he could help out?

330
00:13:42.054 --> 00:13:43.115
[Sighs]

331
00:13:43.215 --> 00:13:44.717
I mean. he did.

332
00:13:44.817 --> 00:13:46.639
but I don't think Cliff's
the type of person

333
00:13:46.739 --> 00:13:48.041
we want helping us.

334
00:13:48.141 --> 00:13:50.484
Besides. Jordan
hasn't made a decision.

335
00:13:50.584 --> 00:13:52.082
We don't even know
which way he's leaning.

336
00:13:52.106 --> 00:13:54.148
Is there any way that
we can find out?

337
00:13:58.673 --> 00:14:00.576
[Doorbell rings]

338
00:14:00.676 --> 00:14:02.098
Amina. hi!

339
00:14:02.198 --> 00:14:03.940
Coop: Hey. champ.
Preach: Hey.

340
00:14:04.040 --> 00:14:05.662
Layla: Wow. Amina.
I haven't seen you

341
00:14:05.762 --> 00:14:07.104
since your first day back.

342
00:14:07.204 --> 00:14:08.385
Well. here I am.

343
00:14:08.485 --> 00:14:11.028
[Music playing]
OK. Um. how...

344
00:14:11.128 --> 00:14:13.591
or how is it? Are you...
are you loving it out there?

345
00:14:13.691 --> 00:14:16.034
I mean. there's not
a lot to tell. So...

346
00:14:16.134 --> 00:14:20.119
Coop: Uh. what ever happened
to the paper you was writing?

347
00:14:20.219 --> 00:14:22.602
Well. some idiots at
the school paper

348
00:14:22.702 --> 00:14:24.484
don't know what good writing is.

349
00:14:24.584 --> 00:14:26.006
I doubt they even read it.

350
00:14:26.106 --> 00:14:27.648
They definitely
read it. all right.

351
00:14:27.748 --> 00:14:29.210
[Both chuckle]

352
00:14:29.310 --> 00:14:31.613
Breonna: Has Coop told you
that I'm a Boardley Bear?

353
00:14:31.713 --> 00:14:33.896
Boardley's their rival.
by the way.

354
00:14:33.996 --> 00:14:35.498
I had the best time at school.

355
00:14:35.598 --> 00:14:37.340
I bet you can't wait
to get back.

356
00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:38.461
[Chuckles]

357
00:14:38.561 --> 00:14:40.103
I'd leave right now if I could.

358
00:14:40.203 --> 00:14:41.304
[Chuckles]

359
00:14:41.404 --> 00:14:43.147
[Chuckles softly]

360
00:14:43.247 --> 00:14:46.471
Um. are... are you in town
for long or...?

361
00:14:46.571 --> 00:14:47.952
Just a few more days.

362
00:14:48.052 --> 00:14:50.796
I still have that dead week
to study before finals.

363
00:14:50.896 --> 00:14:53.359
Really? Wow! A dead week.

364
00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:56.042
I had friends at Dinsberg.
It was intense.

365
00:14:56.142 --> 00:14:57.964
They never had a dead week.

366
00:14:58.064 --> 00:15:00.928
Amina: Friends? I thought
you said you were rivals.

367
00:15:01.028 --> 00:15:03.211
Breonna: In sports. yeah.
but not in real life.

368
00:15:03.311 --> 00:15:05.734
They were lucky if they
had two days to study.

369
00:15:05.834 --> 00:15:07.175
Guess it's a new thing.
[Chuckles]

370
00:15:07.275 --> 00:15:09.378
You know how progressive
Dinsberg says they are.

371
00:15:09.478 --> 00:15:10.860
Right.

372
00:15:10.960 --> 00:15:13.543
Amina: If you will excuse me.
Preach: Mm-hmm.

373
00:15:13.643 --> 00:15:15.645
Sorry.

374
00:15:18.849 --> 00:15:20.712
Dog. you notice
anything off about Amina

375
00:15:20.812 --> 00:15:22.354
since she been back?

376
00:15:22.454 --> 00:15:23.755
I've barely seen her all week.

377
00:15:23.855 --> 00:15:25.197
That's the point.

378
00:15:25.297 --> 00:15:27.235
I mean. don't it seem like
she been trying to avoid us?

379
00:15:27.259 --> 00:15:29.238
Nah. she just busy. Nothing
wrong with working hard.

380
00:15:29.262 --> 00:15:31.324
I like to think she
learned that from me.

381
00:15:31.424 --> 00:15:33.064
Preach. she was so excited
about Dinsberg.

382
00:15:33.146 --> 00:15:34.728
and now every time we
bring it up.

383
00:15:34.828 --> 00:15:36.090
she get upset.

384
00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:37.211
Red flag?

385
00:15:37.311 --> 00:15:38.853
Maybe something
happened at school?

386
00:15:38.953 --> 00:15:40.695
Coop: Whatever it is.
I think it's

387
00:15:40.795 --> 00:15:42.798
something she ain't telling us.

388
00:15:51.168 --> 00:15:53.511
Amina: OK.

389
00:15:53.611 --> 00:15:55.473
What kind of food is this?

390
00:15:55.573 --> 00:15:56.875
Uh. barbecue fusion.

391
00:15:56.975 --> 00:15:58.473
Khalil: What's that?
Amina: Rich people food.

392
00:15:58.497 --> 00:16:00.479
Coop: Excuse me?
Layla: Well. it looks amazing.

393
00:16:00.579 --> 00:16:02.742
I can't wait.
Jordan: Yes.

394
00:16:04.744 --> 00:16:07.487
Coop: Ooh.

395
00:16:07.587 --> 00:16:08.889
Where are we supposed to sit?

396
00:16:08.989 --> 00:16:10.589
Oh. we figured it'd get
a little crowded.

397
00:16:10.671 --> 00:16:12.854
so we set up on the side
patio for you and Khalil.

398
00:16:12.954 --> 00:16:16.098
Yeah. I... I think we've
outgrown the kids' table.

399
00:16:16.198 --> 00:16:17.579
We'll sit here.

400
00:16:17.679 --> 00:16:19.382
[Indistinct chatter]

401
00:16:19.482 --> 00:16:22.385
Amina: See? Plenty of room.

402
00:16:22.485 --> 00:16:24.147
Khalil: Mm. So cozy.

403
00:16:24.247 --> 00:16:27.912
Well. I would like to make
a little toast to Coop.

404
00:16:28.012 --> 00:16:30.114
I hope you guys are just
as proud of her as I am.

405
00:16:30.214 --> 00:16:31.877
Jordan: Taught her
everything she knows.

406
00:16:31.977 --> 00:16:35.521
[Laughter]

407
00:16:35.621 --> 00:16:37.479
Preach: Well. as long as
we're talking about proud...

408
00:16:37.503 --> 00:16:38.885
Dad. don't.

409
00:16:38.985 --> 00:16:40.283
You better get used to me
being proud of you.

410
00:16:40.307 --> 00:16:41.768
You're gonna do
some great things.

411
00:16:41.868 --> 00:16:43.871
And Dinsberg is just the start.

412
00:16:45.673 --> 00:16:47.015
Cheers.

413
00:16:47.115 --> 00:16:50.138
You know. your school has
a really good pre-law club.

414
00:16:50.238 --> 00:16:52.581
if you ever wanted to follow
in Coop's footsteps.

415
00:16:52.681 --> 00:16:54.904
Yeah. No offence. but
I want to help our people.

416
00:16:55.004 --> 00:16:56.426
not corporations.

417
00:16:56.526 --> 00:16:58.104
Coop: Amina. if you want
to sit with the adults.

418
00:16:58.128 --> 00:16:59.830
you need to act like one.

419
00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:01.952
No. babe. that's fair.

420
00:17:02.052 --> 00:17:04.391
Representing corporations is
a big part of what my firm does.

421
00:17:04.415 --> 00:17:06.878
Same goes for the firm
Coop's interning with.

422
00:17:06.978 --> 00:17:09.001
That's true.
But once she graduates

423
00:17:09.101 --> 00:17:11.163
and we're able to open
our own firm.

424
00:17:11.263 --> 00:17:13.166
eventually we will
be able to focus

425
00:17:13.266 --> 00:17:15.008
on giving back
to the community more.

426
00:17:15.108 --> 00:17:16.330
Eventually. Right.
My bad.

427
00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:17.811
I just assumed people stayed

428
00:17:17.911 --> 00:17:19.511
in their high-paying
jobs until they were

429
00:17:19.593 --> 00:17:21.055
rich enough to retire on a beach

430
00:17:21.155 --> 00:17:22.657
and don't care anymore.

431
00:17:22.757 --> 00:17:23.917
Yeah. Tell that to
Mrs. Baker.

432
00:17:23.999 --> 00:17:25.180
Jordan: To be fair.

433
00:17:25.280 --> 00:17:26.938
I'm pretty sure she
is on a beach right now.

434
00:17:26.962 --> 00:17:28.344
You know what?
I have an idea.

435
00:17:28.444 --> 00:17:29.986
Why don't we talk about
something else?

436
00:17:30.086 --> 00:17:31.468
That's a great idea. babe.

437
00:17:31.568 --> 00:17:32.669
probably one of your best.

438
00:17:32.769 --> 00:17:33.969
Amina. I have barely seen you.

439
00:17:34.051 --> 00:17:35.352
Tell me all about Dinsberg.

440
00:17:35.452 --> 00:17:38.396
You know. this table is
a little crowded.

441
00:17:38.496 --> 00:17:40.498
Come on. Khalil.

442
00:17:52.272 --> 00:17:54.331
I'm guessing you haven't
told your pops about Dinsberg.

443
00:17:54.355 --> 00:17:55.777
What gave it away?

444
00:17:55.877 --> 00:17:58.220
His speech about how proud
of me he is?

445
00:17:58.320 --> 00:17:59.862
He'll still be proud of you.

446
00:17:59.962 --> 00:18:01.744
Maybe not right away.

447
00:18:01.844 --> 00:18:03.426
but you need to tell him. Amina.

448
00:18:03.526 --> 00:18:06.129
I know. I'm just waiting
for the right time.

449
00:18:07.330 --> 00:18:09.149
And right now in front of
all of his friends is

450
00:18:09.173 --> 00:18:10.835
certainly not that time.

451
00:18:10.935 --> 00:18:13.518
I get that. but you
gotta do it soon.

452
00:18:13.618 --> 00:18:15.080
He's gonna find out. Amina.

453
00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:16.522
Khalil. why do you even care?

454
00:18:16.622 --> 00:18:18.824
I thought we weren't friends
anymore. right?

455
00:18:23.950 --> 00:18:25.412
[Adults laugh]

456
00:18:25.512 --> 00:18:26.654
So what did London say

457
00:18:26.754 --> 00:18:27.971
when you turned down
his job offer?

458
00:18:27.995 --> 00:18:29.377
Mm. Not so loud.

459
00:18:29.477 --> 00:18:31.295
Coop: Wait. Is this the job
offer Layla told me about?

460
00:18:31.319 --> 00:18:33.822
Yes. London offered me
the head coach job at Beverly.

461
00:18:33.922 --> 00:18:35.224
but Khalil does not know.

462
00:18:35.324 --> 00:18:37.587
so please just
keep it down. all right?

463
00:18:37.687 --> 00:18:39.189
Coop: I wish I didn't know.

464
00:18:39.289 --> 00:18:40.666
I mean. this is gonna
ruin things with Cassius.

465
00:18:40.690 --> 00:18:42.272
And you're abandoning
your wife on tour?

466
00:18:42.372 --> 00:18:44.675
Coop. I can speak for myself.

467
00:18:44.775 --> 00:18:46.135
Are you seriously
considering this?

468
00:18:46.217 --> 00:18:47.675
I thought you didn't
want drama tonight.

469
00:18:47.699 --> 00:18:50.322
Can we not talk about
the offer or Cassius?

470
00:18:50.422 --> 00:18:51.563
[Doorbell rings]

471
00:18:51.663 --> 00:18:53.165
Singer: ♪ All for you.
all for you ♪

472
00:18:53.265 --> 00:18:54.585
♪ You. you. you.
and you. too... ♪

473
00:18:54.627 --> 00:18:56.289
Layla: No. Jordan
didn't tell me

474
00:18:56.389 --> 00:18:58.109
he invited you over
to work on the showcase.

475
00:18:58.191 --> 00:18:59.791
Jordan: I didn't think
you would show up.

476
00:18:59.873 --> 00:19:01.856
especially after I saw
who you were meeting with.

477
00:19:01.956 --> 00:19:04.058
KJ: You guys. uh.
having a party?

478
00:19:04.158 --> 00:19:06.461
Cassius: Yeah. it looks like
you're celebrating something.

479
00:19:06.561 --> 00:19:08.904
Big decision maybe?

480
00:19:09.004 --> 00:19:10.186
It's just dinner.

481
00:19:10.286 --> 00:19:11.646
In fact. now that
you two are here.

482
00:19:11.727 --> 00:19:12.789
you should stay.

483
00:19:12.889 --> 00:19:14.831
Yeah. I could eat.

484
00:19:14.931 --> 00:19:17.975
I'm not sure
there's enough room.

485
00:19:19.176 --> 00:19:21.279
Let's hear it for
the cool kids' table. huh?

486
00:19:21.379 --> 00:19:22.601
[Barks]

487
00:19:22.701 --> 00:19:23.802
Give me something.

488
00:19:23.902 --> 00:19:25.164
[Chuckles weakly]
No?

489
00:19:25.264 --> 00:19:27.046
Uh. KJ. did your dad
tell you about

490
00:19:27.146 --> 00:19:29.168
all the new recruiters coming
to the showcase?

491
00:19:29.268 --> 00:19:33.013
Yeah. My dad tells me
everything you're up to.

492
00:19:33.113 --> 00:19:35.135
OK.

493
00:19:35.235 --> 00:19:41.383
Um. Amina. did you do
anything interesting today?

494
00:19:41.483 --> 00:19:43.145
Please say yes.

495
00:19:43.245 --> 00:19:46.349
Let's see. Today.
I stopped by your school.

496
00:19:46.449 --> 00:19:49.673
where I had the sweetest.
sweetest conversation

497
00:19:49.773 --> 00:19:51.155
with my dear friend Khalil.

498
00:19:51.255 --> 00:19:52.833
I'm a terrible friend
and a terrible daughter.

499
00:19:52.857 --> 00:19:54.038
I am the problem here.

500
00:19:54.138 --> 00:19:55.680
After that. I went home
to study.

501
00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:57.540
but then my dad forced me
to come here. so...

502
00:19:57.622 --> 00:19:59.004
[Chuckles]

503
00:19:59.104 --> 00:20:02.048
Wait. You went home
after South Crenshaw?

504
00:20:02.148 --> 00:20:03.730
Yeah. Is that OK with you?

505
00:20:03.830 --> 00:20:05.171
I'm sorry.

506
00:20:05.271 --> 00:20:06.432
Is there something going on
I don't know about?

507
00:20:06.433 --> 00:20:07.694
You know. Coach. I don't know.

508
00:20:07.794 --> 00:20:08.896
Is there. Amina?

509
00:20:08.996 --> 00:20:11.519
OK. you know what.
this is ridiculous.

510
00:20:13.441 --> 00:20:14.783
Sorry. You... you can
have that.

511
00:20:14.883 --> 00:20:17.486
Amina: Nope. It's fine.

512
00:20:32.224 --> 00:20:34.406
Preach: Bet you don't
eat this good at school.

513
00:20:34.506 --> 00:20:36.168
Breonna: I know I didn't.

514
00:20:36.268 --> 00:20:39.332
Can we please not
talk about school?

515
00:20:39.432 --> 00:20:42.496
Sorry. I... I thought
tonight was

516
00:20:42.596 --> 00:20:44.338
supposed to be
a study break for me.

517
00:20:44.438 --> 00:20:48.063
Great idea. Amina.
No more boring school talk.

518
00:20:48.163 --> 00:20:49.544
Coop: Look. how about
we talk about

519
00:20:49.644 --> 00:20:51.066
all this great food
Breonna brought?

520
00:20:51.166 --> 00:20:52.606
Breonna: I can't take
all the credit.

521
00:20:52.648 --> 00:20:54.470
Coop said she used to love
this as a kid.

522
00:20:54.570 --> 00:20:56.473
Really? Coop said
she loved

523
00:20:56.573 --> 00:20:58.435
umami-infused rib bites
as a kid?

524
00:20:58.535 --> 00:21:00.775
Layla: You know. we don't need
to talk about food either.

525
00:21:00.858 --> 00:21:01.858
Or talk at all.

526
00:21:01.899 --> 00:21:03.081
Fine by me. all right?

527
00:21:03.181 --> 00:21:04.438
How about we all
just finish our meals

528
00:21:04.462 --> 00:21:05.924
without any more...
[Doorbell rings]

529
00:21:06.024 --> 00:21:08.367
Come on!

530
00:21:08.467 --> 00:21:10.469
Now what?

531
00:21:13.193 --> 00:21:14.935
Tori: I hope I'm not
interrupting.

532
00:21:15.035 --> 00:21:16.457
I just wanted to stop by

533
00:21:16.557 --> 00:21:18.639
and give this packet to Khalil.

534
00:21:21.442 --> 00:21:25.467
KJ? I didn't know
you were here.

535
00:21:25.567 --> 00:21:28.191
Just full of
surprises. aren't you?

536
00:21:28.291 --> 00:21:30.393
KJ: Um. yeah. yeah.

537
00:21:30.493 --> 00:21:32.195
It all just kind of
happened last minute.

538
00:21:32.295 --> 00:21:37.362
I see. It actually smells
really good in here.

539
00:21:37.462 --> 00:21:40.045
Tori. you want to join us?

540
00:21:40.145 --> 00:21:42.147
Sure.

541
00:21:42.508 --> 00:21:44.510
Welcome to the kids' table.

542
00:21:46.512 --> 00:21:48.575
So catch me up.
What'd I miss?

543
00:21:48.675 --> 00:21:50.377
Khalil: Well.
KJ was gonna tell us

544
00:21:50.477 --> 00:21:52.259
about his trip to the Bay.

545
00:21:52.359 --> 00:21:55.143
Oh. great. KJ's barely told
me anything about it. So...

546
00:21:55.243 --> 00:21:57.245
Hmm.

547
00:21:59.127 --> 00:22:01.430
I mean. um...

548
00:22:01.530 --> 00:22:03.152
nothing really happened.

549
00:22:03.252 --> 00:22:05.475
I just hung out with my mom.

550
00:22:05.575 --> 00:22:09.640
I... saw some friends.
It was... it was cool.

551
00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:11.803
Yeah. KJ's mom lives
pretty close to Dinsberg.

552
00:22:11.903 --> 00:22:13.324
right. Amina?

553
00:22:13.424 --> 00:22:15.006
Surprised you two
didn't hook up.

554
00:22:15.106 --> 00:22:17.810
I mean. it's like an hour away.

555
00:22:17.910 --> 00:22:19.812
That's a lot of time.

556
00:22:19.912 --> 00:22:22.275
Time reveals truth. right?

557
00:22:25.519 --> 00:22:26.941
[Breonna and Coop chuckle]

558
00:22:27.041 --> 00:22:29.344
Breonna: You know. I wish you
could've seen Coop

559
00:22:29.444 --> 00:22:31.266
hold her own
with the other lawyers.

560
00:22:31.366 --> 00:22:32.366
She was like a rock star.

561
00:22:32.407 --> 00:22:33.949
Not surprising.

562
00:22:34.049 --> 00:22:35.707
I mean. it ain't no
different than being onstage.

563
00:22:35.731 --> 00:22:37.309
You just got to get
the crowd rooting for you.

564
00:22:37.333 --> 00:22:38.555
and then. boom. mic drop.

565
00:22:38.655 --> 00:22:39.956
More like gavel drop.
[Laughter]

566
00:22:40.056 --> 00:22:42.239
Coop: Very nice.

567
00:22:42.339 --> 00:22:43.721
Cassius: Hey. I got to say.

568
00:22:43.821 --> 00:22:45.399
these might be the best
wings I've ever had.

569
00:22:45.423 --> 00:22:46.925
Did you know that they
vent the boxes?

570
00:22:47.025 --> 00:22:48.687
Clutch move.

571
00:22:48.787 --> 00:22:50.289
Hey. listen. real quick.

572
00:22:50.389 --> 00:22:52.029
I just want to say that
I know this dinner

573
00:22:52.111 --> 00:22:53.492
didn't go exactly as planned.

574
00:22:53.592 --> 00:22:55.735
And if that doorbell
rings one more time.

575
00:22:55.835 --> 00:22:57.377
I'm probably gonna
lose it. but...

576
00:22:57.477 --> 00:22:58.899
it really means a lot

577
00:22:58.999 --> 00:23:00.119
to me that you guys are here

578
00:23:00.200 --> 00:23:02.103
and I just...
Preach: Amina!

579
00:23:02.203 --> 00:23:05.627
You must've lost your damn mind.

580
00:23:05.727 --> 00:23:08.711
I give up.

581
00:23:08.811 --> 00:23:11.114
I just got off the phone
with your dean at Dinsberg.

582
00:23:11.214 --> 00:23:12.555
but apparently. I've already had

583
00:23:12.655 --> 00:23:14.658
a long talk with him yesterday.

584
00:23:16.580 --> 00:23:19.484
Is there something
you need to tell me?

585
00:23:19.584 --> 00:23:22.247
Amina: Um...
Preach: Speak up.

586
00:23:22.347 --> 00:23:24.349
Amina: Um...

587
00:23:25.270 --> 00:23:26.612
[Softly]
There's no dead week.

588
00:23:26.712 --> 00:23:28.775
Preach: I can't hear you.

589
00:23:28.875 --> 00:23:30.256
There's no dead week.

590
00:23:30.356 --> 00:23:33.260
I wrote an article
calling out Dinsberg

591
00:23:33.360 --> 00:23:36.183
for staying silent
after an ICE raid.

592
00:23:36.283 --> 00:23:37.705
They wouldn't let me publish it.

593
00:23:37.805 --> 00:23:41.189
so I released it anonymously
online anyway.

594
00:23:41.289 --> 00:23:45.254
Now I'm suspended
pending expulsion.

595
00:23:51.422 --> 00:23:53.925
So you've been lying
to us this whole time?

596
00:23:54.025 --> 00:23:55.487
Coop. I got this.

597
00:23:55.587 --> 00:23:57.267
So you've been lying
to us this whole time?

598
00:23:57.309 --> 00:23:58.450
Coop: Well said.

599
00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:00.653
What the hell were you thinking?

600
00:24:00.753 --> 00:24:02.375
I was thinking that Dinsberg.

601
00:24:02.475 --> 00:24:03.933
a school that's already
on stolen land.

602
00:24:03.957 --> 00:24:06.580
said nothing when ICE
took their custodian.

603
00:24:06.680 --> 00:24:08.818
But I guess I'm the only one
who cares about that. right?

604
00:24:08.842 --> 00:24:10.901
Well. I guess I'm the only one
who cares about your future.

605
00:24:10.925 --> 00:24:12.947
'cause you threw it away
so damn casually.

606
00:24:13.047 --> 00:24:15.150
Hold on. Preach. I know
you're upset. I am. too.

607
00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:17.313
But she just stood up for
something she believed in.

608
00:24:17.413 --> 00:24:18.714
Didn't you teach her that?

609
00:24:18.814 --> 00:24:20.356
I didn't teach her to lie to me.

610
00:24:20.456 --> 00:24:21.994
OK. I'm just saying.
there's nothing wrong

611
00:24:22.018 --> 00:24:23.720
with doing what you
think is right.

612
00:24:23.820 --> 00:24:25.803
I mean. Breonna. help me out.

613
00:24:25.903 --> 00:24:29.888
Breonna: Honestly. I understand
where Preach is coming from.

614
00:24:29.988 --> 00:24:31.570
That didn't help.

615
00:24:31.670 --> 00:24:33.932
Breonna: Listen. opportunities
like Dinsberg.

616
00:24:34.032 --> 00:24:37.417
they don't come around often
for Black girls like us. so...

617
00:24:37.517 --> 00:24:38.738
I'm nothing like you.

618
00:24:38.838 --> 00:24:40.238
I'm trying to make
a difference now.

619
00:24:40.320 --> 00:24:41.880
not in 10 years.
when it'll be too late.

620
00:24:41.962 --> 00:24:43.540
Well. the only thing you
gonna do is go home

621
00:24:43.564 --> 00:24:45.026
and go to your room.

622
00:24:45.126 --> 00:24:46.668
And just one last thing.

623
00:24:46.768 --> 00:24:49.912
Which one of you fools
pretended to be me. huh?

624
00:24:50.012 --> 00:24:51.313
Khalil knows better.

625
00:24:51.413 --> 00:24:52.791
And my son wouldn't
do anything so...

626
00:24:52.815 --> 00:24:54.918
KJ: It was me.
Cassius: dumb.

627
00:24:55.018 --> 00:24:56.840
Oh. OK. Denzel.

628
00:24:56.940 --> 00:24:59.083
How about you drop one
of your Preach gems?

629
00:24:59.183 --> 00:25:00.644
No. how about this?

630
00:25:00.744 --> 00:25:03.448
Pretend that I'm yelling
at a kid who's in trouble.

631
00:25:03.548 --> 00:25:07.092
OK. let's take it easy
on poor KJ.

632
00:25:07.192 --> 00:25:08.410
He's been telling so many lies.

633
00:25:08.434 --> 00:25:09.874
he probably can't
keep them straight.

634
00:25:09.915 --> 00:25:11.377
Um. Tori. let's go
get some air. OK?

635
00:25:11.477 --> 00:25:12.779
Nope. I'm good.
[Chuckles]

636
00:25:12.879 --> 00:25:15.142
You sure there's nothing
you want to tell me. KJ?

637
00:25:15.242 --> 00:25:16.864
Or you. Amina?

638
00:25:16.964 --> 00:25:20.588
KJ: Hey. um. can we maybe
go talk in private?

639
00:25:20.688 --> 00:25:22.190
What kind of private?

640
00:25:22.290 --> 00:25:23.552
Private like the conversation

641
00:25:23.652 --> 00:25:25.274
you had in the hallway
with Amina earlier

642
00:25:25.374 --> 00:25:29.519
or private like the dance you
had with Amina at Dinsberg?

643
00:25:29.619 --> 00:25:32.282
Yeah. I found this on
the Dinsberg website:

644
00:25:32.382 --> 00:25:34.565
#loveacrosstime.

645
00:25:34.665 --> 00:25:36.447
Y'all see?
[Chuckles]

646
00:25:36.547 --> 00:25:40.051
Yeah. there are a few.
but this one.

647
00:25:40.151 --> 00:25:42.154
this one's my favourite.

648
00:25:45.077 --> 00:25:47.701
KJ: Look. I'm sorry that
I didn't tell you.

649
00:25:47.801 --> 00:25:49.703
but I only went because
it was an emergency.

650
00:25:49.803 --> 00:25:52.787
What kind of emergency has
you rushing over to Dinsberg?

651
00:25:52.887 --> 00:25:54.889
Well. she needed a date
for her dance.

652
00:25:56.371 --> 00:25:57.873
[Chuckles]

653
00:25:57.973 --> 00:26:00.596
Look. she organised
the whole thing.

654
00:26:00.696 --> 00:26:02.278
and... and she spent
so much time

655
00:26:02.378 --> 00:26:03.920
setting it up that.

656
00:26:04.020 --> 00:26:05.482
look. she had no one to go with.

657
00:26:05.582 --> 00:26:07.684
It's only an emergency
if it's your girlfriend.

658
00:26:07.784 --> 00:26:09.787
Or if you. like...

659
00:26:14.392 --> 00:26:16.095
Just tell me the truth.

660
00:26:16.195 --> 00:26:18.197
Did something happen?

661
00:26:24.885 --> 00:26:26.627
I can't believe I trusted you.

662
00:26:26.727 --> 00:26:28.425
Tori. I'm sorry. OK?
It was a stupid mistake.

663
00:26:28.449 --> 00:26:30.231
Khalil: Is there anybody
you not lying to?

664
00:26:30.331 --> 00:26:31.909
I know you like to make
everything about you. Khalil.

665
00:26:31.933 --> 00:26:33.435
but this isn't.
so stay out of it.

666
00:26:33.535 --> 00:26:34.837
Did y'all sleep together?

667
00:26:34.937 --> 00:26:36.479
KJ: What? No.
Amina: No.

668
00:26:36.579 --> 00:26:37.997
Why should I believe
anything that you say?

669
00:26:38.021 --> 00:26:39.581
We all know Amina's
a professional liar.

670
00:26:39.663 --> 00:26:41.685
Just ask her dad.

671
00:26:41.785 --> 00:26:43.007
Hey. can we just...

672
00:26:43.107 --> 00:26:44.809
can we just go talk
someplace else?

673
00:26:44.909 --> 00:26:47.732
Jordan: OK. guys. let's just
relax for a minute. OK?

674
00:26:47.832 --> 00:26:49.334
I'm sure KJ did not mean...

675
00:26:49.434 --> 00:26:50.816
I don't need you to talk for me.

676
00:26:50.916 --> 00:26:52.578
In fact. I don't need
you talking to me.

677
00:26:52.678 --> 00:26:54.220
Whoa. Jordan was
just trying...

678
00:26:54.320 --> 00:26:55.898
Nah. nah. You keep talking
about Coach like that. bro.

679
00:26:55.922 --> 00:26:57.184
we gonna have a issue.

680
00:26:57.284 --> 00:26:58.665
Oh. your coach.

681
00:26:58.765 --> 00:27:00.343
I guess he didn't tell
you about his job offer

682
00:27:00.367 --> 00:27:01.509
to go coach at Beverly.

683
00:27:01.609 --> 00:27:03.611
Say what?

684
00:27:06.535 --> 00:27:09.138
Coach. is that true?

685
00:27:10.259 --> 00:27:12.702
[Exhales]
Yeah.

686
00:27:16.547 --> 00:27:17.888
How could you not tell me

687
00:27:17.988 --> 00:27:19.450
you're leaving for Beverly?

688
00:27:19.550 --> 00:27:21.212
Did you know about this?

689
00:27:21.312 --> 00:27:22.614
Yes. I did. but I just...

690
00:27:22.714 --> 00:27:24.292
Jordan: Look. I didn't want
to say anything

691
00:27:24.316 --> 00:27:25.578
until it was for sure.

692
00:27:25.678 --> 00:27:26.998
Cassius: Oh.
so it's for sure now?

693
00:27:27.079 --> 00:27:28.861
Coop: Look. nothing is
definite yet.

694
00:27:28.961 --> 00:27:30.664
We can do damage control
with Dinsberg.

695
00:27:30.764 --> 00:27:33.587
Right. I am sure that
if Amina just apologises.

696
00:27:33.687 --> 00:27:34.949
they would be open to...

697
00:27:35.049 --> 00:27:36.591
Amina: Wait.
I'm not apologising

698
00:27:36.691 --> 00:27:38.233
if I didn't do anything wrong.

699
00:27:38.333 --> 00:27:40.151
Preach: You sure? 'Cause I
can think of a few things.

700
00:27:40.175 --> 00:27:42.558
KJ: Look. I know
I messed up. It was dumb.

701
00:27:42.658 --> 00:27:44.320
And yet what I still
haven't heard is

702
00:27:44.420 --> 00:27:46.042
that it didn't mean anything.

703
00:27:46.142 --> 00:27:47.760
Khalil: Just tell me the truth.
Are you going to Beverly?

704
00:27:47.784 --> 00:27:49.166
Cassius:
Just be honest for once.

705
00:27:49.266 --> 00:27:51.004
Layla: To be fair. I...
Jordan: Unlike you...

706
00:27:51.028 --> 00:27:53.170
I have been nothing but upfront
since the beginning.

707
00:27:53.270 --> 00:27:55.774
You are the one who's sneaking
around with Cliff Mosely

708
00:27:55.874 --> 00:27:57.816
unless that was KJ
doing another impression.

709
00:27:57.916 --> 00:27:59.698
Are you really working
with that scum?

710
00:27:59.798 --> 00:28:00.699
Considering it.

711
00:28:00.799 --> 00:28:01.901
So if you go to Beverly.

712
00:28:02.001 --> 00:28:03.339
does that mean
I'm coming with you?

713
00:28:03.363 --> 00:28:04.900
KJ: What. and take my spot?
Yeah. keep dreaming.

714
00:28:04.924 --> 00:28:06.466
He's not taking your spot.

715
00:28:06.566 --> 00:28:08.264
-So you are taking my job?
-So you're leaving me behind.

716
00:28:08.288 --> 00:28:09.430
Jordan: I didn't say that!

717
00:28:09.530 --> 00:28:11.050
Amina: You're not even
listening to me.

718
00:28:11.092 --> 00:28:12.714
Won't you even read the article?

719
00:28:12.814 --> 00:28:15.077
If you wanted me to read it.
I would've read it already.

720
00:28:15.177 --> 00:28:17.199
Now you're gonna write
a letter to Dinsberg

721
00:28:17.299 --> 00:28:18.761
saying how sorry you are.

722
00:28:18.861 --> 00:28:20.443
That I will read.

723
00:28:20.543 --> 00:28:23.006
Until then. I don't wanna
hear another word from you.

724
00:28:23.106 --> 00:28:25.449
Hey. easy. Preach. Don't you
think that's a little harsh?

725
00:28:25.549 --> 00:28:27.171
No. I think Preach
is just...

726
00:28:27.271 --> 00:28:29.053
This is none of your business.

727
00:28:29.153 --> 00:28:30.856
I'm sure you'd be
the first in line

728
00:28:30.956 --> 00:28:32.538
to defend ICE if you could.

729
00:28:32.638 --> 00:28:34.019
Layla: Enough. OK?

730
00:28:34.119 --> 00:28:36.222
This has gotten way out of hand.
even for this house.

731
00:28:36.322 --> 00:28:39.165
Everyone go to a corner
and cool off.

732
00:28:41.048 --> 00:28:43.050
Now!

733
00:29:03.194 --> 00:29:05.016
Hey. you leaving?

734
00:29:05.116 --> 00:29:06.178
[Sighs]

735
00:29:06.278 --> 00:29:08.100
Look. I don't need
to cool down. man.

736
00:29:08.200 --> 00:29:09.502
And since KJ is

737
00:29:09.602 --> 00:29:11.344
suddenly so interested
in private schools.

738
00:29:11.444 --> 00:29:13.606
he needs to go home and study.

739
00:29:19.293 --> 00:29:21.976
I'm sorry about tonight.

740
00:29:23.098 --> 00:29:25.281
But maybe we can meet up
tomorrow.

741
00:29:25.381 --> 00:29:27.844
I mean. we do still have
a showcase to plan.

742
00:29:27.944 --> 00:29:30.006
I think I've heard enough
about your plans. man.

743
00:29:30.106 --> 00:29:34.692
OK. I don't know how much
you really know about Cliff.

744
00:29:34.792 --> 00:29:38.737
but he was gone from
the booster club for years

745
00:29:38.837 --> 00:29:40.699
for a reason.

746
00:29:40.799 --> 00:29:42.942
I wouldn't trust anything
that man says.

747
00:29:43.042 --> 00:29:44.784
And I wouldn't trust London.

748
00:29:44.884 --> 00:29:47.046
His loyalty is fickle.

749
00:29:49.650 --> 00:29:51.772
So what now?

750
00:29:53.054 --> 00:29:54.632
After everything.
we're just gonna go back

751
00:29:54.656 --> 00:29:56.858
to hating each other?

752
00:29:59.661 --> 00:30:01.664
I'll see you at the showcase.

753
00:30:08.031 --> 00:30:10.254
Where are you going?

754
00:30:10.354 --> 00:30:13.819
I'm not sure.
I haven't decided yet.

755
00:30:13.919 --> 00:30:17.663
OK. I'm sorry
you found out this way.

756
00:30:17.763 --> 00:30:19.585
OK. I didn't want
to say anything

757
00:30:19.685 --> 00:30:21.988
because nothing is certain.
Khalil.

758
00:30:22.088 --> 00:30:23.871
But you're considering it.

759
00:30:23.971 --> 00:30:28.276
I am. Yeah.
It ju... it just. listen.

760
00:30:28.376 --> 00:30:31.960
nothing will change
between us. I promise.

761
00:30:32.060 --> 00:30:34.283
But you can't promise that.

762
00:30:34.383 --> 00:30:36.325
If you're coaching at Beverly.

763
00:30:36.425 --> 00:30:38.428
you'll be competing against me.

764
00:30:39.789 --> 00:30:41.532
It'll be your job
to make sure I lose.

765
00:30:41.632 --> 00:30:43.174
So explain to me.

766
00:30:43.274 --> 00:30:45.276
how is that not
gonna change things?

767
00:30:47.759 --> 00:30:50.382
[Door opens]

768
00:30:50.482 --> 00:30:52.485
[Door shuts]

769
00:30:55.168 --> 00:30:57.631
You definitely found
the best corner.

770
00:30:57.731 --> 00:30:59.994
You know.
I was gonna go outside.

771
00:31:00.094 --> 00:31:02.316
but that Tori girl
went that way.

772
00:31:02.416 --> 00:31:03.478
She kinda scares me.

773
00:31:03.578 --> 00:31:07.122
Well. look. I... I am sorry
about tonight.

774
00:31:07.222 --> 00:31:09.645
I know it was a lot
different than our Ojai trip.

775
00:31:09.745 --> 00:31:11.648
I know. right?
Thank God.

776
00:31:11.748 --> 00:31:12.885
But I thought you
had a good time.

777
00:31:12.909 --> 00:31:14.291
I did with you.

778
00:31:14.391 --> 00:31:16.493
But you know what else is
great about Ojai. babe?

779
00:31:16.593 --> 00:31:18.135
Pools and spas.

780
00:31:18.235 --> 00:31:20.979
You know what we saw
none of? Pools or spas.

781
00:31:21.079 --> 00:31:23.021
At least your friends
know how to have fun.

782
00:31:23.121 --> 00:31:25.664
Fun? They argued
the entire time.

783
00:31:25.764 --> 00:31:27.667
If I didn't love
hearing people argue.

784
00:31:27.767 --> 00:31:29.349
I wouldn't be a lawyer.

785
00:31:29.449 --> 00:31:32.352
Your friends are just
passionate. I like 'em.

786
00:31:32.452 --> 00:31:34.155
Even Amina?

787
00:31:34.255 --> 00:31:37.118
I still think she
could be a great lawyer.

788
00:31:37.218 --> 00:31:39.080
But that was a family issue

789
00:31:39.180 --> 00:31:41.123
that I was gonna stay out of

790
00:31:41.223 --> 00:31:43.205
until someone asked me
what I thought

791
00:31:43.305 --> 00:31:46.209
and then got upset when I
didn't agree with her.

792
00:31:46.309 --> 00:31:47.971
You figured that out. huh?

793
00:31:48.071 --> 00:31:49.413
You're a good lawyer.

794
00:31:49.513 --> 00:31:53.137
More like I'm just good
at reading you.

795
00:31:53.237 --> 00:31:56.181
Preach and I. we've always
had each other's backs.

796
00:31:56.281 --> 00:31:58.263
And at the time we didn't.

797
00:31:58.363 --> 00:32:00.987
I just hoped it'd be you
that did.

798
00:32:01.087 --> 00:32:03.389
I'm sorry it felt like that.

799
00:32:03.489 --> 00:32:05.712
but you're never going
to have somebody's back

800
00:32:05.812 --> 00:32:08.035
by just agreeing with
everything they say.

801
00:32:08.135 --> 00:32:09.957
So I get to disagree
with you now.

802
00:32:10.057 --> 00:32:11.559
Of course. of course.

803
00:32:11.659 --> 00:32:14.443
Listen. no one understands
what Preach has been through

804
00:32:14.543 --> 00:32:15.844
more than you.

805
00:32:15.944 --> 00:32:18.888
He's had to fight for
everything his whole life.

806
00:32:18.988 --> 00:32:21.010
And I think he just wants
better for Amina.

807
00:32:21.110 --> 00:32:22.893
There is nothing wrong
with that.

808
00:32:22.993 --> 00:32:24.935
Oh. You are
a good lawyer.

809
00:32:25.035 --> 00:32:26.617
[Both chuckle]

810
00:32:26.717 --> 00:32:28.539
Thank you.

811
00:32:28.639 --> 00:32:29.781
Thank you.

812
00:32:29.881 --> 00:32:32.044
[Chuckles]

813
00:32:48.984 --> 00:32:51.247
I hope you know how sorry I am.

814
00:32:51.347 --> 00:32:54.931
I'm not sure I know you
at all anymore.

815
00:32:55.031 --> 00:32:57.534
Please. Would you
just read the article?

816
00:32:57.634 --> 00:32:59.577
I know you'll understand.

817
00:32:59.677 --> 00:33:01.579
Is there anything
in that article that says

818
00:33:01.679 --> 00:33:07.446
it's OK to lie to me.
to my face repeatedly?

819
00:33:08.888 --> 00:33:10.950
I thought we had
a good relationship.

820
00:33:11.050 --> 00:33:14.154
I thought we trusted each other.

821
00:33:14.254 --> 00:33:16.637
I was gonna tell you tonight.

822
00:33:16.737 --> 00:33:18.239
but then dinner happened.

823
00:33:18.339 --> 00:33:23.024
What about the other times
in the 3 days you been home?

824
00:33:26.388 --> 00:33:28.892
Look. I wanted
to tell you the truth

825
00:33:28.992 --> 00:33:31.895
so many times.

826
00:33:31.995 --> 00:33:34.919
I was just afraid
how you'd react.

827
00:33:37.842 --> 00:33:38.904
[Exhales]

828
00:33:39.004 --> 00:33:42.047
After everything
we been through...

829
00:33:43.809 --> 00:33:48.555
it just sucks that you
didn't think I'd understand.

830
00:33:48.655 --> 00:33:51.979
And that broke my heart.

831
00:34:05.916 --> 00:34:08.339
I'm guessing you don't want
to hear my Preach impression

832
00:34:08.439 --> 00:34:09.660
right now.

833
00:34:09.760 --> 00:34:11.763
Good guess.

834
00:34:13.325 --> 00:34:17.430
Look. I shouldn't
have argued with you

835
00:34:17.530 --> 00:34:18.871
in front of Amina.

836
00:34:18.971 --> 00:34:21.595
That's my fault.
That was a family issue.

837
00:34:21.695 --> 00:34:25.179
Nah. You family. Coop.

838
00:34:28.703 --> 00:34:30.205
I appreciate you.

839
00:34:30.305 --> 00:34:33.289
But you know the good thing
about family is

840
00:34:33.389 --> 00:34:37.253
they forgive you
even when you messed up.

841
00:34:37.353 --> 00:34:39.496
No. She messed up bad.
Coop.

842
00:34:39.596 --> 00:34:42.019
Come on. She ain't
mess up that bad.

843
00:34:42.119 --> 00:34:44.902
Look at me.
Ain't nobody get shot.

844
00:34:45.002 --> 00:34:49.828
Look. I can't say that I ain't
never lied to my parents.

845
00:34:49.928 --> 00:34:52.952
but when I did. it was usually
because I was scared.

846
00:34:53.052 --> 00:34:55.916
That's what Amina is
right now... scared.

847
00:34:56.016 --> 00:34:59.280
And she did something she
thought you would be proud of.

848
00:34:59.380 --> 00:35:00.841
and she got suspended for it.

849
00:35:00.941 --> 00:35:02.844
Am I supposed to be
proud of her for this?

850
00:35:02.944 --> 00:35:04.125
Not at all.

851
00:35:04.225 --> 00:35:07.890
You are supposed to make sure
that she knows

852
00:35:07.990 --> 00:35:09.812
you got her back no matter what

853
00:35:09.912 --> 00:35:12.455
and that she's not
in this alone.

854
00:35:12.555 --> 00:35:16.400
And maybe read the damn article.

855
00:35:22.407 --> 00:35:24.409
Gonna be all right. man.

856
00:35:29.496 --> 00:35:31.498
[Exhales]

857
00:35:36.744 --> 00:35:38.747
[Dog barks]

858
00:35:44.994 --> 00:35:47.137
[Sighs]

859
00:35:47.237 --> 00:35:48.298
What'd you think?

860
00:35:48.398 --> 00:35:50.140
It was really good.

861
00:35:50.240 --> 00:35:51.880
I just wish I was
the first one to read it

862
00:35:51.922 --> 00:35:53.424
instead of the last.

863
00:35:53.524 --> 00:35:55.527
Yeah.

864
00:35:56.888 --> 00:35:59.271
I do. too.

865
00:35:59.371 --> 00:36:02.275
So you saw ICE take them
and nobody tried to stop it?

866
00:36:02.375 --> 00:36:04.037
Nobody did a thing.

867
00:36:04.137 --> 00:36:05.238
[Exhales]

868
00:36:05.338 --> 00:36:06.600
Man. you gonna find out

869
00:36:06.700 --> 00:36:10.244
this world is full of people
that are vindictive.

870
00:36:10.344 --> 00:36:13.648
stupid. scared.
and all of the above.

871
00:36:13.748 --> 00:36:16.211
But you've got to be
better than them.

872
00:36:16.311 --> 00:36:18.174
Dad. I just couldn't
stay silent.

873
00:36:18.274 --> 00:36:19.856
Well. you don't have
to be silent.

874
00:36:19.956 --> 00:36:22.018
Just be smart.

875
00:36:22.118 --> 00:36:24.181
You think I'm cool
with every decision

876
00:36:24.281 --> 00:36:27.625
my bosses at South Crenshaw
High School make?

877
00:36:27.725 --> 00:36:31.390
But I don't quit.
I don't get myself fired

878
00:36:31.490 --> 00:36:33.953
because I know I can do
more good for those kids

879
00:36:34.053 --> 00:36:35.474
if I stay.

880
00:36:35.574 --> 00:36:37.454
And everyone at Dinsberg
is always talking about

881
00:36:37.497 --> 00:36:39.760
how we're one big family.

882
00:36:39.860 --> 00:36:42.563
Once I realised that was a lie.

883
00:36:42.663 --> 00:36:44.245
I just...

884
00:36:44.345 --> 00:36:46.488
I got so angry.

885
00:36:46.588 --> 00:36:47.729
I get it.

886
00:36:47.829 --> 00:36:51.053
But every fight is
not your fight.

887
00:36:51.153 --> 00:36:53.536
Right now I just need
for you to be 16

888
00:36:53.636 --> 00:36:57.140
and not take on the world's
problems all by yourself.

889
00:36:57.240 --> 00:37:00.985
and I promise we'll get
through this together.

890
00:37:01.085 --> 00:37:03.949
No snooty school's gonna
mess up my girl's future.

891
00:37:04.049 --> 00:37:06.271
[Chuckles]

892
00:37:06.371 --> 00:37:08.494
Thank you. Dad.

893
00:37:13.019 --> 00:37:16.043
But for now. you are grounded.

894
00:37:16.143 --> 00:37:18.766
You do not leave this house
without me by your side.

895
00:37:18.866 --> 00:37:20.208
You hear me?

896
00:37:20.308 --> 00:37:21.369
Yes.

897
00:37:21.469 --> 00:37:24.012
Consider me like
an ankle bracelet.

898
00:37:24.112 --> 00:37:28.137
You get too far away. I go off.

899
00:37:28.237 --> 00:37:29.779
You hear me?

900
00:37:29.879 --> 00:37:31.882
Yes. sir.

901
00:37:34.285 --> 00:37:35.867
Love you. old man.

902
00:37:35.967 --> 00:37:38.189
I love you. too.

903
00:37:38.289 --> 00:37:40.372
[Chuckles]

904
00:37:42.054 --> 00:37:43.876
Singer:
♪ Is this what you wanted? ♪

905
00:37:43.976 --> 00:37:46.439
♪ You can fake it.
I can fake it hardly... ♪

906
00:37:46.539 --> 00:37:48.882
He said he hasn't decided yet.

907
00:37:48.982 --> 00:37:50.284
But will by this weekend.

908
00:37:50.384 --> 00:37:51.681
I mean. if he ain't
turn it down by now.

909
00:37:51.705 --> 00:37:53.708
he's probably not going to.

910
00:37:54.589 --> 00:37:56.291
Hey. but don't sweat it. man.

911
00:37:56.391 --> 00:37:58.013
A superstar like you gonna have

912
00:37:58.113 --> 00:37:59.975
a bunch of coaches in your life.

913
00:38:00.075 --> 00:38:02.458
But you only got one family.

914
00:38:02.558 --> 00:38:04.621
Jordan was the whole
reason I made QB.

915
00:38:04.721 --> 00:38:07.144
If he leaves. what's
gonna happen to my spot?

916
00:38:07.244 --> 00:38:08.421
He ain't the one
with the power. man.

917
00:38:08.445 --> 00:38:09.907
He ain't in charge.

918
00:38:10.007 --> 00:38:13.231
Coach Bobby knows who the best
player on the team is.

919
00:38:13.331 --> 00:38:15.774
Ain't that right?

920
00:38:17.817 --> 00:38:19.679
That's right.

921
00:38:19.779 --> 00:38:21.781
I'm really glad you called.

922
00:38:23.824 --> 00:38:25.806
I'm not promising anything.

923
00:38:25.906 --> 00:38:27.288
You don't have to.

924
00:38:27.388 --> 00:38:29.290
I'm just glad you knew
we'd be here for you

925
00:38:29.390 --> 00:38:31.393
when you needed us.

926
00:38:34.316 --> 00:38:36.599
I'mma get us something to drink.

927
00:38:44.288 --> 00:38:46.111
What'd I tell you?

928
00:38:46.211 --> 00:38:47.712
I knew Baker was gonna screw up.

929
00:38:47.812 --> 00:38:49.915
Our son is hurting right now.

930
00:38:50.015 --> 00:38:52.017
It's nothing to celebrate.

931
00:39:04.352 --> 00:39:06.375
Um. thanks for staying
to help clean.

932
00:39:06.475 --> 00:39:08.377
No problem.
It's the least I could do.

933
00:39:08.477 --> 00:39:09.819
I mean. dinner was my idea.

934
00:39:09.919 --> 00:39:11.381
And it's not like I'm in a rush

935
00:39:11.481 --> 00:39:12.903
to get home to Preach and Amina.

936
00:39:13.003 --> 00:39:15.426
I saw you and Breonna made up.

937
00:39:15.526 --> 00:39:17.928
You really should get
a wall in this kitchen.

938
00:39:20.331 --> 00:39:21.793
She said she had a fun time.

939
00:39:21.893 --> 00:39:23.435
which is not the word
I would use

940
00:39:23.535 --> 00:39:24.757
to describe tonight.

941
00:39:24.857 --> 00:39:26.319
The night didn't go as planned.

942
00:39:26.419 --> 00:39:27.520
but it was still a success.

943
00:39:27.620 --> 00:39:29.082
No. I wouldn't use
that word either.

944
00:39:29.182 --> 00:39:31.445
Look. Breonna had fun
with your friends.

945
00:39:31.545 --> 00:39:33.407
and everybody likes her

946
00:39:33.507 --> 00:39:35.449
and is really excited
for you two.

947
00:39:35.549 --> 00:39:37.692
including me.

948
00:39:37.792 --> 00:39:40.976
I'm sorry that I
questioned your happiness.

949
00:39:41.076 --> 00:39:42.818
It's all good.

950
00:39:42.918 --> 00:39:44.941
I mean. you were just
looking out. right?

951
00:39:45.041 --> 00:39:49.026
Plus. I hear that's
what good friends do.

952
00:39:49.126 --> 00:39:51.469
Yes. And good friends
support each other

953
00:39:51.569 --> 00:39:52.870
no matter what.

954
00:39:52.970 --> 00:39:54.472
I'm really glad you're happy.

955
00:39:54.572 --> 00:39:56.575
Thank you.

956
00:40:06.747 --> 00:40:08.169
Hiding in the bushes?

957
00:40:08.269 --> 00:40:09.887
You've gone from liar
to stalker really quickly.

958
00:40:09.911 --> 00:40:11.408
I was just waiting
for you to get home.

959
00:40:11.432 --> 00:40:12.734
Not helping your stalker case.

960
00:40:12.834 --> 00:40:14.817
I just wanted to
talk to you in private.

961
00:40:14.917 --> 00:40:17.019
I don't have
anything else to say to you.

962
00:40:17.119 --> 00:40:18.581
As far as I'm concerned.

963
00:40:18.681 --> 00:40:21.905
you and Amina are both liars.
who deserve each other.

964
00:40:22.005 --> 00:40:25.669
There is nothing going on
between me and Amina.

965
00:40:25.769 --> 00:40:27.311
It was one mistake.

966
00:40:27.411 --> 00:40:29.314
Singer: ♪ True I'm unstable ♪

967
00:40:29.414 --> 00:40:30.534
♪ Picking up the pieces... ♪

968
00:40:30.615 --> 00:40:32.558
Tori. please. you know me.

969
00:40:32.658 --> 00:40:34.360
Or you know I'm not
that type of guy

970
00:40:34.460 --> 00:40:36.002
that lies and cheats.

971
00:40:36.102 --> 00:40:37.724
OK. it was really a mistake.

972
00:40:37.824 --> 00:40:40.087
We got caught up
in a stupid moment

973
00:40:40.187 --> 00:40:41.929
and... and it didn't even
mean anything.

974
00:40:42.029 --> 00:40:45.814
Look. it'll never happen again.

975
00:40:45.914 --> 00:40:50.139
Singer: ♪ Hope you think
of me often... ♪

976
00:40:50.239 --> 00:40:51.981
You know what's sad?

977
00:40:52.081 --> 00:40:56.847
Is I can't tell if you're
lying to me or to yourself.

978
00:40:58.328 --> 00:40:59.670
Whatever.

979
00:40:59.770 --> 00:41:02.273
I don't care anymore.

980
00:41:02.373 --> 00:41:03.955
Bye. KJ.

981
00:41:04.055 --> 00:41:05.055
Wait. Tori...

982
00:41:05.137 --> 00:41:07.920
Singer:
♪ Tryin' to stay whole ♪

983
00:41:08.020 --> 00:41:12.205
♪ I'm just tryin'
to stay whole ♪

984
00:41:12.305 --> 00:41:14.167
Oh. for sure.

985
00:41:14.267 --> 00:41:16.250
Piece of cake. Yeah.

986
00:41:16.350 --> 00:41:17.772
He's here now.

987
00:41:17.872 --> 00:41:20.575
Yeah. I'll get back to you.

988
00:41:20.675 --> 00:41:22.778
Oh. wow.

989
00:41:22.878 --> 00:41:26.222
I got to tell you.
I am so glad you called me.

990
00:41:26.322 --> 00:41:28.745
It seems not everyone is onboard

991
00:41:28.845 --> 00:41:30.347
with London's decision.

992
00:41:30.447 --> 00:41:32.489
And do you know what that means?

993
00:41:34.091 --> 00:41:36.935
We can finally get rid
of Jordan Baker.

994
00:41:50.310 --> 00:41:52.874
Where do we start?

995
00:42:21.748 --> 00:42:23.750
Greg. move your head.

995
00:42:24.305 --> 00:43:24.167
